error[MODE-1]: this operation requires a global value: `x` is the caller's storage, but the result must be global
 --> ../../conformance/MODE/MODE-1-mut-result-bad.hir:6:3
   6 |   x
     |   ^ 
 --> ../../conformance/MODE/MODE-1-mut-result-bad.hir:5:15
   5 | fn get(mut x: Bytes) -> Bytes {
     |               ^^^^^ provided: `x` is a `mut` parameter, local to the caller
 --> ../../conformance/MODE/MODE-1-mut-result-bad.hir:5:25
   5 | fn get(mut x: Bytes) -> Bytes {
     |                         ^^^^^ required: the result names no `in ..` source, so it is global (MODE-7)
  = help: 1. declare the result `in x` (no cost; signature)
  = help: 2. `unique x` (deep copy: allocates, costs O(size), and is not allowed under `@noalloc`)
  = help: 3. declare the parameter `take x` (changes meaning: the caller loses `x`)
  = note: `copy x` does not help: a copy shares the blocks of `x`, which stay local
